JIZURA lyric stage
https://github.com/852wa/JIZURA/

The JavaScript in this directory is the stage engine from src/ of that project
(planner, renderer, styles, and the expression packs). It is licensed under
the MIT License. Copyright (c) 2026 hakoniwa. See LICENSE in this directory.

Not included: the editor UI (src/12_ui.js), MP4 export (src/11_export.js),
After Effects tooling, and vendor/mp4-muxer. Fonts are loaded from Google
Fonts when a frame is drawn; they are not bundled here.

RyanMusic plays this engine from the song's lyric times. The files stay
separate and are concatenated in filename order when the app is built, the
same order JIZURA's own build uses.

RyanMusic changes:
- 09_render.js: live playback can skip the full-frame glow. Copying the finished
  frame back to blur it costs most of a frame, so the player sets noBloom.
  Playback also asks for every frame (koma 0, 60fps) instead of the 12fps step.
